    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option C (\"The extreme intensification of physical strain caused by excessively long workdays\")\n\n• Audio Evidence & Breakdown:\nFactory worker Sébastien warns: \"we worked nearly nine-hour days standing on packing conveyor lines... production paces became unbearable and musculoskeletal injuries spiked... a trap for factory workers' health\".\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options & Refutations):\n  - Option A (Freezing cold night shifts) [INCORRECT - WEATHER HAZARD DISTRACTOR]: The issue is daily shift length, not cold weather or night scheduling.\n  - Option B (Toxic chemical solvent exposure) [INCORRECT - UNRELATED CHEMICAL HAZARD]: The manufacturing facility is food packaging, and risks are ergonomic strain.\n  - Option C (Intensification of physical strain from long shifts) [CORRECT]: Captures the core reality that compressing identical production quotas into 9-hour shifts damages physical health.\n  - Option D (Reduction in statutory sick pay) [INCORRECT - SOCIAL SECURITY RED HERRING]: Statutory sickness compensation benefits are never referenced."
